  "round": 3,
  "prompt": "What is the VAT treatment of the sale of a residential lot valued at ₱1.9 million?",
  "runtimeCommit": "87ce0c7571f9bd57514b6c2dfb45e9427d19c6b6",
  "answer": "### Short Answer\nThe sale of a residential lot valued at ₱1.9 million is subject to VAT because it exceeds the threshold of ₱1.5 million for residential lots, as specified in the National Internal Revenue Code (NIRC).\n\n### Controlling Authorities\n- **RR 16-2005**: Implements the VAT provisions and specifies that sales of residential lots exceeding ₱1.5 million are subject to VAT.\n\n### Interpretation\n\n### Practical Meaning\nFor the sale of the residential lot valued at ₱1.9 million, the seller must charge VAT at the applicable rate (currently 12%) on the sale price. This means that the seller will need to issue a VAT invoice and remit the VAT collected to the Bureau of Internal Revenue (BIR). Buyers should be aware that the total cost will include VAT, which is an additional expense on top of the selling price.",
